SUMMARY:Explore the Berryessa Snow Mountain National Monument Region
DESCRIPTION:Learn more about this fascinating landscape\, located just west and north of Davis in the northern Coast Ranges. Bob Schneider\, coauthor of the recently published guidebook titled \, Exploring the Berryessa Snow Mountain National Monument Region\, will share the wonders of this landscape\, one shaped by ancient tectonic forces\, uplifted ocean crust\, and volcanic seamounts that have drawn the attention of geologists from around the world. Beyond its scientific significance\, the monument offers rugged beauty\, diverse wildlife habitats\, scenic hiking opportunities\, and traces of California’s rich mining heritage. The difficult history of our region’s diverse Indigenous Peoples in the area is told. Their new guidebook is well-illustrated\, tells captivating stories\, and provides detailed maps and route descriptions that allow you to explore the region on your own.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/explore-the-berryessa-snow-mountain-national-monument-region/
LOCATION:Mary L. Stephens – Davis Branch Library\, 315 E. 14th Street\, Davis\, C\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Books & Talks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Picture1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Mary L. Stephens Davis Branch Library":MAILTO:Lana.Harman@yolocounty.org
END:VEVENT
